Changing employee guidelines must update the instructions used for employee tasks.

Changing manager guidelines must update instructions used for manager tasks.

Changing HOD guidelines must update instructions used for HOD tasks.

Changing a company-wide guideline must affect all relevant roles and tasks.

Changing platform-specific guidelines must affect only relevant platform tasks, without accidentally changing unrelated companies' configurations.

## 19. Saving and generation failure behavior

Saving company details and generating prompts are related operations but must not cause data loss.

First preserve the valid company profile/guidelines in persistent storage.

If the AI API is temporarily unavailable:

- Keep the successfully saved profile or guidelines.
- Do not display a false "AI instructions updated successfully" message.
- Mark the new prompt configuration as needing generation or refresh.
- Show a clear status and a Retry button.
- Retry with reasonable limits and handle rate limits/timeouts using the existing client where possible.
- Do not leave the company permanently stuck in an unusable state.
- Do not silently keep using an old prompt version that contradicts the latest saved guidelines.

When an old instruction set no longer matches the current saved policy, the runtime must not pretend it is current. Either assemble a compact safe instruction directly from the latest saved data using a supported fallback, or clearly pause the affected AI operation until a valid current configuration can be prepared.

Never lose the last successfully saved company information merely because prompt generation failed.

Use the smallest reliable implementation compatible with the existing architecture. Do not introduce an unnecessary complex queue or service if the current project can handle this safely.

